  "chunks": [
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Graphic Design (التصميم الجرافيكي) — Bachelor (BA) study plan 2025/2026, Faculty of Engineering & Design, Middle East University.\nThe degree requires 135 credit hours in total:\n- University requirements: 18 credit hours (compulsory)\n- University electives: 6 credit hours\n- Faculty requirements: 24 credit hours (group A: 6, group C: 18 — design foundations)\n- Area of study (major) requirements: 81 credit hours\n- Area of study (major) electives: 6 credit hours\nThere are no ancillary courses in this plan. Remedial courses are taken only when required and are not counted in the 135 hours.\nThe plan includes Field Training (6 credit hours, 320 training hours, after passing 90 credit hours) and a two-part graduation project (Graduation Project 1 requires Designing Integrated Advertising Campaigns and 90 passed credit hours)."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Graphic Design study plan 2025/2026 — approvals and signatories.\nFaculty Council decision 02/06-2025/2026, adopted 06/11/2025. Deans' Council decision 05/15-2025/2026, adopted 30/12/2025.\nHead of Department: Dr. Sattar Al-Juboori. Dean of the Faculty: Prof. Ayman Abdel Salam Awad. Director of Admissions and Registration: Mrs. Nadia Al-Bakri."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Graphic Design — creative and digital courses in the 2025/2026 study plan:\nComputer Graphics (التصميم الجرافيكي بالحاسوب), Digital Photography, Illustration, Arabic and Latin Typography, Logo Design and Application, Advertising Design, Infographic Design, 2D & 3D Animation (الرسوم المتحركة ثنائية وثلاثية الأبعاد), Packaging Design, Designing Integrated Advertising Campaigns, Digital Media Design, Web Design and Application Interfaces, Visual Communication Theories. Electives include Electronic Advertising and Marketing, Environmental Graphic Design, Design of Newspapers, Magazines and Electronic Publishing, Commercial Photography and Printmaking."
    }
  ],
